title=How+to+Paint+Glowing+Plasma+Effects+on+Miniatures&slug=glowing-plasma-effects&content=%3Ch1%3EHow+to+Paint+Glowing+Plasma+Effects+on+Miniatures%3C%2Fh1%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EShort+answer%3A%3C%2Fstrong%3E+Block+in+the+glow+with+a+dark+base%2C+add+a+midtone+halo+around+the+light+source%2C+then+build+a+gradient+of+three+brighter+tones+toward+the+centre+and+finish+with+pinpoint+white+highlights.+Add+reflected+glow+on+nearby+surfaces+%E2%80%94+that+final+step+is+what+makes+plasma+effects+look+real+instead+of+painted-on.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cblockquote+class%3D%22wp-block-quote%22%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3EDisclosure%3A+Some+links+on+this+page+are+affiliate+links+%E2%80%94+if+you+buy+through+them%2C+we+may+earn+a+small+commission+at+no+extra+cost+to+you.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Fblockquote%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EWhat+You+Need%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3EPrimer+%28black+or+very+dark+grey+%E2%80%94+glow+needs+a+dark+canvas%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EBase+colour+for+the+glow+core+%28e.g.+deep+blue+or+violet%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E2%E2%80%933+lighter+shades+of+the+same+hue+%28up+to+near-white+for+the+hottest+point%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EA+dark+contrast+colour+for+the+surrounding+areas%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EFine+detail+brush+%28%230+or+%231%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EOptional%3A+glaze+medium+for+smooth+transitions%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+1%3A+Choose+the+Light+Source%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EDecide+%3Cem%3Ebefore%3C%2Fem%3E+painting+where+the+light+comes+from%3A+a+plasma+coil%2C+a+weapon+barrel%2C+glowing+eyes%2C+or+a+portal.+One+clear+source+beats+three+confused+ones.+Mark+the+spot+with+a+dot+of+the+brightest+colour+%E2%80%94+this+is+your+anchor+for+the+entire+gradient.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+2%3A+Block+In+the+Glow%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EPaint+the+whole+glow+area+in+your+darkest+tone+of+the+effect+colour.+Around+it%2C+sketch+the+midtone+halo+%E2%80%94+the+zone+that+will+catch+the+light.+Keep+edges+rough+at+this+stage%3B+you%27ll+clean+them+up+with+the+gradient.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+3%3A+Build+the+Gradient%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EWork+from+the+outside+in%3A+darkest+at+the+edges%2C+brighter+toward+the+source.+Thin+paint%2C+multiple+passes.+The+transition+zone+between+two+shades+should+be+soft+%E2%80%94+drybrush+or+glaze+the+boundary+if+you+see+a+hard+step.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+4%3A+Add+Reflected+Light%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EThis+is+the+step+most+beginners+skip+%E2%80%94+and+the+one+that+sells+the+effect.+Take+your+midtone+and+add+a+few+thin+streaks+on+surfaces+%3Cem%3Enear%3C%2Fem%3E+the+source%3A+adjacent+panels%2C+the+weapon+housing%2C+the+ground+below.+If+a+surface+would+catch+that+light+in+reality%2C+it+needs+a+hint+of+it.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+5%3A+Final+Highlights%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3ETiny%2C+sharp+dots+of+near-white+at+the+very+core.+Small+is+critical+%E2%80%94+a+big+white+blob+kills+the+illusion+in+one+brushstroke.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3ECommon+Mistakes%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EToo+bright+too+early%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+you+can+always+add+brightness%2C+but+you+can%27t+remove+it%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3ESkipping+reflected+light%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+number-one+reason+glow+looks+flat%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EWarm+and+cool+mixed%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+pick+one+hue+family+per+effect+%28green+glow+%3D+green+reflections%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EGiant+cores%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+plasma+coils+are+thin%3B+keep+the+hottest+point+small%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EThe+Warpstorm+Twist%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EGive+your+models+the+Warpstorm+signature%3A+paint+the+glow+in+%3Cstrong%3Estorm-green%2Fturquoise%3C%2Fstrong%3E+or+%3Cstrong%3Eviolet+portal-light%3C%2Fstrong%3E%2C+then+use+the+same+hue+for+the+reflected+light+on+armour+panels.+A+squad+painted+with+a+shared+glow+colour+reads+as+one+coherent+force+from+across+the+table+%E2%80%94+and+matches+the+Warpstorm+aesthetic+perfectly.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3ERecommended+Paints+and+Tools%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cfigure+class%3D%22wp-block-table%22%3E%3Ctable%3E%3Cthead%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Cth%3EItem%3C%2Fth%3E%3Cth%3EWhy%3C%2Fth%3E%3Cth%3ELevel%3C%2Fth%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3C%2Fthead%3E%3Ctbody%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3EStarter+acrylic+set+%28blues%2Fviolets%2Fgreens%29%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3ECovers+every+glow+hue+you+need%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EBeginner%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3EGlaze+medium%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3ESmooths+gradients+without+re-thinning%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EIntermediate%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3EKolinsky+detail+brush+%230%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3ESharp+pinpoint+highlights%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EAll%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3EWet+palette%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EKeeps+thin+glow+mixes+workable+for+hours%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EAll%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3C%2Ftbody%3E%3C%2Ftable%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3E%28Affiliate+links+%E2%80%94+buy+through+them+to+support+more+guides.%29%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EFAQ%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EIs+OSL+%28object+source+lighting%29+the+same+as+painting+glow%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EOSL+is+the+broader+technique+%E2%80%94+painted+glow+is+its+simplest+form.+True+OSL+adds+reflected+light+on+all+surrounding+surfaces%3B+this+guide+includes+that+in+Step+4.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EWhich+colours+work+best+for+beginner+plasma+effects%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EGreen+and+teal+are+the+most+forgiving+%E2%80%94+they%27re+bright%2C+contrast+strongly+with+dark+bases%2C+and+a+slightly+uneven+blend+still+looks+intentional.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3ECan+I+paint+glow+effects+over+a+light+primer%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EIt+works+but+fights+you%3A+glow+relies+on+dark+surroundings+for+contrast.+Prime+dark%2C+or+paint+a+dark+zone+around+the+glow+first.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EHow+do+I+make+multiple+glowing+units+look+consistent%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EMix+one+batch+of+each+shade+on+a+wet+palette+and+paint+all+units+in+one+session.+Consistency+between+squads+is+what+makes+an+army+glow+look+deliberate.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EContinue+on+the+Workbench%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Feasy-weathering-techniques%2F%22%3EEasy+Weathering+Techniques+for+Miniatures%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+perfect+partner+to+glow+effects%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Fobject-source-lighting%2F%22%3EObject+Source+Lighting%3A+Simple+OSL+Guide%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+advanced+version+of+this+technique%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Fbest-hobby-tools%2F%22%3EBest+Hobby+Tools+for+Miniature+Painting%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+brushes+and+lamps+that+make+this+easier%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Flore%2Fwhat-is-the-warpstorm%2F%22%3EWhat+Is+the+Warpstorm%3F%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+lore+behind+the+storm-green+glow%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Cblockquote+class%3D%22wp-block-quote%22%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EPaint+one+test+model+before+the+squad.%3C%2Fstrong%3E+Ten+minutes+on+a+single+miniature+saves+three+hours+of+repainting.+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fshop%2Fpaints%2F%22%3EGet+the+glow+palette+%E2%86%92%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%3Cem%3E%28affiliate+links%29%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Fblockquote%3E&status=publish